  "2026-10-26T05:41:17.393Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: strict complete3119-item all-status corpus, refreshed open/in_progress lists, two request-specific searches, full live release reliability and publication-fence owners, plus Git introduction6fc2dd060 identify shipped registry acceptance lineage rather than an existing orchestration-envelope defect. New bounded child tracks the actual October26 timeout; no closed feature is reopened."
  "2026-10-26T05:51:54.350Z","harness:codex","Exact operational proof: original parent40265600223 attempt1 cancelled at05:35:30Z after110minutes. Child40269172902 independently passed all nine Linux/macOS/Windows by npm-local/npm-global/Bun acceptance legs and advertised2026.10.26 at05:35:55Z. A manual rerun of the same parent, attempt2, succeeded at05:46 UTC through existing-tag verification: it reused child40269172902 and immutable commit46fd91415. No second tag or publication occurred. Strengthened existing workflow-budget test fails against110minutes; the bounded180minute envelope passes, reserving60preparation+30queues+unchanged60/15/5children+10orchestration. All121 focused native tests, TypeScript targets, build and permission checks pass; full static and linked evidence follow."
  "2026-10-26T09:54:58.317Z","harness:codex","Review-test refinement: the prior contract actually passes with the parent temporarily set to170minutes, proving it omits the documented10minute orchestration reserve. Strengthen the existing arithmetic assertion to include that reserve: the same170minute control now fails at required180. Restore the production workflow to its unchanged180minute limit immediately after the isolated test. No child timeout, publication guard or quality policy changes."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-26T05:51:07.427Z","harness:codex",A waiting parent workflow needs separate wall-time reserves for local preparation and aggregate runner queues; child execution limits alone do not bound orchestration duration.
